<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss government launches new bond tender.</title>
<headline>Swiss government launches new bond tender.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss government said it will reopen an outstanding 4-1/2 percent bond, maturing June 10, 2007, in a new bond tender  SWIW.</p>
<p>The government will take bids of a maximum one billion Swiss francs, it said.</p>
<p>Final terms will be announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bond is fungible with the outstanding issue  CH470458= (value number 470 458).</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
